<details><summary>What this 3D view can and cannot tell you</summary><p><strong>Measured range, not a certified printer gamut.</strong> The optional surface is a convex hull around only the selected measured points. It excludes standards, unmeasured CMYK candidates and model estimates. A small set near one color is a local test range, not the full ATEXCO gamut. A hull may bridge untested colors, and being inside it is not a printability guarantee.</p><p><strong>Numeric tolerance is different from gamut.</strong> The wireframe sphere is the CIE76 distance boundary around the standard. Under a strict ΔE76 &lt; 2 rule, the surface itself does not pass. Camera rotation does not change the calculated distance. The displayed plot has no automatic in-gamut / out-of-gamut classifier.</p><p><strong>Measurement conditions matter.</strong> Only compare data under matching conditions. An imported set must be confirmed against the current master snapshot before pass/fail is displayed; known D65/D50, observer, mode, backing or preparation conflicts block this comparison. Metadata is not a conversion. Schematic Lab colors use a D65/2-degree display approximation and clipping solely to orient the eye; the coordinates and numerical results are not changed.</p></details>
